<body>
    <h1>Meeting Minutes of 2026/08/04 - Q2 reporting</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"814e836be223">Hi all,</p>
<p local-id=3D"14c728b5cb16">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"250807b435cc">Thank you so much for your attendance. Please =
kindly check the meeting minutes below for the meeting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a88e1e520f03">Date: Monday, 3rd August, 2026</p>
<p local-id=3D"210ac2bc6908">Time: 17:30 HK time</p>
<p local-id=3D"ef1275f8cc07">Attendees:Tao Huang, Loura Guo, Vincent, Jiaji=
n Zhong, Daijiang Xie, Yixi Wang,Guangyuan Mu, Huifang Liu, Jiaxing Dai</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"2af280213029" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
QuickRecap">Quick Recap</h2>
<p local-id=3D"535c5524639e">This meeting focused on weekly progress update=
s, technical discussions, and research sharing across different project lay=
ers. Huifang Liu introduced a research paper on<strong>&nbsp;language reinf=
orcement learning and self-reflection mechanisms</strong>, explaining how r=
eflection-based architectures can help agents identify execution errors and=
 improve future task performance through components such as the action mode=
l, evaluator, and self-reflection model.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c3b60361cc23">Jiajin Zhong reported progress on <strong>Conf=
luence integration and PPT parsing </strong>development, including successf=
ul Confluence API access, meeting-record Q&amp;A testing, and discussions a=
round API permissions and document parsing optimization.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"be104c97e935">Guangyuan Mu presented upgrades to the data pr=
ocessing pipeline, including <strong>semantic segmentation, topic clusterin=
g, and graph-based card generation</strong>, which aim to improve retrieval=
 performance and multi-hop reasoning capabilities.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b2eca6326b55">Jiaxing Dai shared progress on <strong>two-sta=
ge retrieval and ranking functions</strong>. However, current evaluation re=
sults showed unsatisfactory recall performance, leading to discussions on c=
hunking strategies, embedding dimensions, query rewriting, and retrieval op=
timization.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"482b721f0a42">Daijiang Xie and Huifang Liu provided updates =
on the Agent Layer, including intent recognition, query rewriting, routing =
strategies, tool registry, and multi-turn conversation memory.</p>
<p local-id=3D"83f5a6e5d03f">At the end of the meeting, Tao provided severa=
l improvement suggestions, including <strong>preparing a CPR progress demon=
stration</strong>&nbsp;before next Tuesday, researching existing market sol=
utions, improving meeting efficiency, and defining clear objectives and pro=
gress for each module.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"5f9093ba-5dfd-43ea-9477-247dee32ecba" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h1 local-id=3D"c67644d9feb4" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
Follow-upActions">Follow-up Actions</h1>
<h3 local-id=3D"1b93580edf0f" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
YixiWang">Yixi Wang</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"836aaa29-7c20-48cc-abf5-b5a26dd36c7c">
<li local-id=3D"7c3d81d6-13bc-47b3-af35-a7593cfe1f52">
<p local-id=3D"3acbe684d36c">Record and design a <strong>proposal regarding=
 file </strong>update frequency and buffer-layer mechanisms, and prepare <s=
trong>related content for the next-stage</strong>&nbsp;presentation.</p></l=
i>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"f02803448482" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
GuangyuanMu">Guangyuan Mu</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"fa9fe233-80fe-4d01-b9d0-58c63145551d">
<li local-id=3D"d8052b67-624b-4c62-ac40-181b856f6e17">
<p local-id=3D"9a9ee8237af8">Provide a <strong>detailed presentation</stron=
g>&nbsp;in the next meeting using concrete examples and diagrams to explain=
 the upgraded data processing pipeline, including semantic segmentation, to=
pic clustering, graph card generation, and retrieval mechanisms.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1c92273a-f728-4ee3-a877-e23854a93da3">
<p local-id=3D"f409424e2833">Present <strong>evaluation results</strong>&nb=
sp;of the upgraded pipeline.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cb3bddce-2c55-4ca3-96b0-6e2117b7fd11">
<p local-id=3D"21ae54cc13bd">Clearly document this week=E2=80=99s completed=
 work i<strong>n Confluence</strong>, including data pipeline upgrades and =
ranking mechanism improvements.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"5f91cf9c7f47" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
JiajinZhong">Jiajin Zhong</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"61e86371-1a19-4b59-a1bf-879b80364d46">
<li local-id=3D"2fa6cb0f-81ad-4608-8256-d047257f3c47">
<p local-id=3D"bb1c6e56bdc1">Investigate whether the current Confluence int=
egration uses the export function (expo), and evaluate whether an HTML pars=
er should be added to replace the current HTML-to-Word conversion process.<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1072a452-e5ab-498e-b269-22c21e7932d1">
<p local-id=3D"19d59bf4ff46">Communicate with Guangyuan Mu (Confluence spac=
e administrator) to obtain the <strong>required permissions or API </strong=
>for accessing the team Confluence space.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4d9ead1b-a0e5-4d4c-82ef-9eea656c7f73">
<p local-id=3D"cde8c0e89a4c">Research and design an <strong>incremental upd=
ate mechanism</strong>&nbsp;for Confluence content, such as using modificat=
ion history or version numbers, and discuss the design with the team.</p></=
li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"6a5f1ce2925a" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
Collaboration">Collaboration</h3>
<p local-id=3D"4b0865cbce55"><strong>All members:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"ef88b2a0-4b62-4e6d-a0af-3c067ae4fbbd">
<li local-id=3D"e3d6158c-68ab-426c-8a66-d694e3caebdc">
<p local-id=3D"183d0619b190">Discuss and finalize the <strong>appropriate e=
mbedding model </strong>dimension selection to support future retrieval opt=
imization.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"755a022e-345d-4381-9a73-9458233e9b53">
<p local-id=3D"e09bc5149ce7">Continue improving layer-specific functionalit=
y and prepare for upcoming integration demonstrations.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr local-id=3D"efb2030d-211a-4761-944a-a09132766a01" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h1 local-id=3D"907d93ea7e72" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
Summary">Summary</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"c7ec248ee934" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
LanguageReinforcementLearningandSelf-ReflectionDiscussion">Language Reinfor=
cement Learning and Self-Reflection Discussion</h2>
<p local-id=3D"fe76f5930eeb">Huifang Liu shared a research paper related to=
 language reinforcement learning, introducing its architecture and working =
principles, with a focus on how self-reflection mechanisms can improve agen=
t execution processes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1af2e6762504">Tao asked about the difference between reflect=
ion and ReAct. Huifang explained that reflection focuses on identifying spe=
cific execution failures and generating targeted improvement strategies, wh=
ile ReAct represents a broader reasoning-action-observation loop.</p>
<p local-id=3D"cfa8715f44fc">Yixi Wang suggested integrating user feedback =
into the agent=E2=80=99s context to improve future task execution. Tao note=
d that users may not always be willing to provide detailed feedback and sug=
gested reducing user effort through lightweight feedback methods, such as c=
omparison-based selection.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"c553c6d5-cb2b-4deb-858f-4f69ca210ff8" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"4b29d253637b" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
ConfluenceAPIIntegrationandDataProcessingDiscussion">Confluence API Integra=
tion and Data Processing Discussion</h2>
<p local-id=3D"39abbe3901a7">Jiajin Zhong reported two major achievements: =
successful Confluence platform integration, including meeting-record questi=
on-answering tests, and the addition of a PPT parser.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6b7e1b7af11e">During the discussion, the team identified tha=
t the current pipeline converts HTML content into Word documents before par=
sing. Yixi Wang suggested directly introducing an HTML parser to simplify t=
he processing flow.</p>
<p local-id=3D"38f64e534fcc">The team also discussed Confluence API usage a=
nd data pipeline improvements. Jiajin confirmed successful API integration =
and proposed improvements including incremental updates and buffer-layer me=
chanisms. Vincent suggested documenting these design mechanisms for the nex=
t-stage CPR presentation.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"4a7c018d-708f-480a-a15c-425f6671bbf9" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"5c56e89bde3a" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
DataProcessingPipelineUpgrade">Data Processing Pipeline Upgrade</h2>
<p local-id=3D"070afb8f4748">Guangyuan Mu presented a comprehensive upgrade=
 of the data processing pipeline, including pre-compression, semantic segme=
ntation, and topic clustering.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5b76a7e5e5db">The upgraded pipeline generates 333 hybrid-ind=
ex cards and uses graph-based querying mechanisms to improve multi-hop reas=
oning performance.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a33ee72073e3">The team discussed how semantic segmentation a=
nd topic-based clustering could produce more meaningful retrieval units com=
pared with traditional fixed-length chunking methods.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"da38cd2a-3f4b-41c9-9ccd-80781f555a21" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"109b55c9a39e" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
RetrievalQualityandRankingOptimizationDiscussion">Retrieval Quality and Ran=
king Optimization Discussion</h2>
<p local-id=3D"8ffa1c4ff882">Jiaxing Dai shared progress on implementing tw=
o-stage retrieval and ranking functions.</p>
<p local-id=3D"808feca62d23">The current approach first filters relevant fi=
nancial reports and then performs vector retrieval on chunks from the top-r=
anked documents. However, current testing results showed low recall perform=
ance.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e8a49ea8e0a4">The team discussed possible causes, including =
chunking strategies, embedding models, and named entity recognition (NER). =
Tao suggested solving the current recall problem before introducing query r=
ewriting improvements.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eb239e7e376c">Vincent recommended referring to existing rese=
arch papers, datasets, and evaluation methods to improve retrieval performa=
nce.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"209d794e-25a8-4d2f-9744-32f17511bf50" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"100d0b3ac89d" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
MLModelRecallIssueDiscussion">ML Model Recall Issue Discussion</h2>
<p local-id=3D"5272ba7c2d59">The team discussed current recall issues in th=
e retrieval model.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0e148480d016">Vincent pointed out that a recall score below =
0.8 would make the system difficult to use effectively. Jiajin suggested th=
at the issue might come from the chunking layer of the data processing pipe=
line.</p>
<p local-id=3D"142619c72ff1">Yixi Wang mentioned that previous testing achi=
eved approximately 84% recall, suggesting that the current dataset may intr=
oduce additional challenges.</p>
<p local-id=3D"167c418bdafe">Huifang Liu introduced recent Agent Layer prog=
ress, including the complete workflow from frontend requests to answer gene=
ration. Completed functions include query rewriting, routing strategies, an=
d tool registry. Further evaluation and optimization are still required.</p=
>
<hr local-id=3D"27c3f570-72b0-43b7-ae5d-7c2534d29598" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"187e60fba51a" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
KnowledgeBaseFunctionalityDemonstration">Knowledge Base Functionality Demon=
stration</h2>
<p local-id=3D"a286b9ce59f2">Daijiang Xie demonstrated the working principl=
es of intent recognition and query rewriting within the knowledge base syst=
em.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4f20b6f241b9">Using a business-trip reimbursement example, D=
aijiang explained how multiple retrieval rounds and query rewriting can imp=
rove answer efficiency and accuracy.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7f530e27ccad">Tao asked whether these functions require addi=
tional third-party models. Daijiang confirmed that these capabilities are i=
mplemented internally within the Agent system and do not require external m=
odels.</p>
<p local-id=3D"157f89c76770">The team discussed evaluation methods for thes=
e functions, while detailed testing approaches still require further design=
.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"c922590a-125f-49b7-bb6b-394fc551be68" data-layout=3D"wide" =
data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"6e9c297dcbc8" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/08/04-Q2reporting-=
CodeIntegrationandProjectProgressDiscussion">Code Integration and Project P=
rogress Discussion</h2>
<p local-id=3D"e16406d585e4">The team discussed code merging and overall pr=
oject progress.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6c8f01d95151">Yixi Wang agreed to assist with code merging a=
fter the meeting and prepare a demo version for the next presentation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d18f7790d20a">Tao emphasized that each module should clarify=
 its objectives and completion status before next Tuesday. He also encourag=
ed the team to study existing AI system designs in the market.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0c6bf3abcb58">The team further discussed testing requirement=
s for query rewriting functionality. Tao suggested implementing simple unit=
 tests to evaluate rewriting effectiveness.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e98db27e874f"></p>
<p local-id=3D"fd39f6f5c172">Hi <strong>Huijie</strong>,</p>
<p local-id=3D"f319a5c914ba">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"187a5d7450a1">Kindly remind you that <strong>Huijie </strong=
>will be the <strong>host</strong>&nbsp;and <strong>MoM Noter</strong>&nbsp=
;of next weekly meeting. Please read above Notes and get prepared.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9952d4d17a28">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"fbda02400424">Kind regards,</p>
<p local-id=3D"8e6868a3a496"></p>
<p local-id=3D"c625ea4eb31b"><strong>Huifang</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"63ee85a0c3c0"></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
